      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A confirmation alone doesn't change the risk. 1000 mg/day is five times the maximum labeled dose, and I know of no indication that calls for it. An overdose-level dose of sertraline could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, arrhythmia, or other serious harm.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose right away.** Tell me the indication and the dose you want, such as 50 mg or 100 mg PO once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **Help you raise the question with your supervising physician or the pharmacist.** If your attending really does want a dose above 200 mg/day, they should place or co-sign that order themselves and document the rationale. Pharmacy will almost certainly call to verify it.\n\nIf 1000 mg came from a verbal order, a handoff note, or a unit conversion, please recheck the source. Do you want me to enter a standard dose?"
      }
